<h1>Create a study group</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Add a group with a course, meeting information, and member capacity.
</p>

<h2>Step-by-step instructions</h2>
<ol>
  <li>On the main window, click <strong>Create group</strong>.
      A separate form window opens.</li>
  <li>Enter a <strong>Group name</strong>.</li>
  <li>Select a catalog course from the <strong>Course</strong> dropdown.</li>
  <li>Enter a <strong>Description</strong> explaining what the group
      will study.</li>
  <li>Fill in the <strong>Meeting time</strong> and
      <strong>Location</strong>.</li>
  <li>Enter a positive whole number in <strong>Maximum members</strong>.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Save group</strong>. When the form is valid,
      the window closes and the group is added to the current session.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Show all</strong> on the main window to see the
      new group even if previous filters would hide it.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Example values</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Group name</td><td>CS101 Study Crew</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Course</td><td>CS101</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Description</td><td>Review programming concepts and practice course exercises together.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Meeting time</td><td>Mondays at 3 PM</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Location</td><td>Campus library, study room 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Maximum members</td><td>5</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<figure>
  <img src="/images/studyhub-create.png"
       alt="StudyHub create-group form filled with example group and meeting information">
  <figcaption>
    Complete all fields before selecting Save group.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>Correcting invalid input</h2>
<p>
  All fields are required. Text fields cannot contain only spaces,
  a catalog course must be selected, and capacity must be a positive
  integer. Values such as abc, 0, negative numbers, or decimals are invalid.
</p>
<p>
  If validation fails, the form stays open with your entries preserved
  and displays an error. Correct the indicated problem and click
  <strong>Save group</strong> again.
</p>

<h2>Cancel without saving</h2>
<p>
  Click <strong>Cancel</strong> to close the form without adding a group.
</p>

<aside class="notice">
  <strong>Session-only storage:</strong>
  Saving adds the group to the running application's memory.
  It does not save the group permanently; groups reset when StudyHub closes.
</aside>

<p>Next: <a href="/features/delete-group">Delete a group</a></p>

